;; Measurement behind docs/adr/2608300100-jvm-free-residual-kernel.edn.
;;
;; Question: can a real, bit-exactness-critical piece of this repo's H.264
;; decode arithmetic be written in Kotoba guest grammar, compiled through the
;; JDK-free front door, and EXECUTED — agreeing with the .cljc decoder on data
;; that came out of a real bitstream rather than out of someone's head?
;;
;; Method: `java`, `javac`, `clojure` and `clj` are shadowed on PATH by stubs
;; that exit 127 and append to a marker file. The run fails if the marker is
;; ever written, so "no JVM was used" is asserted rather than assumed. Three
;; executions drive the SAME 2-D composition (scripts/kotoba_kernel_common.cljk)
;; and are each compared against the same corpus.
;;
;; Reproduce:
;;   kbb --backend sci --classpath scripts scripts/verify-kotoba-kernel.cljk --amu <amu> [--native]
;;   kbb -M:test -n h264.kotoba-kernel-vectors-test

